<section>
  ## Morph anything

  Not only code: an image, a heading or a diagram with the same `id` in the next section glides from where it was.
  Images with the same file do it on their own. Press → to see it move.

  <img src=diagram.svg class=left width=180px />
</section>

<section>
  ## Same picture, bigger

  <img src=diagram.svg class=right width=460px />

  <text id=note>The picture above is the same file, so it grew and moved by itself. Give a paragraph the same `id` as one in the section before and it glides too.</text>
</section>

<notes>
  Morph pairs items by id between two sections of a slide, or between two slides. Text that changes cross-fades while it moves. The same `id` on `<code>` continues its animation.
</notes>
